@local/session-hub README · Paging：The page renders at most 200 rows at a time and a `Show more` action appends the next batch; the footer states how many rows remain. The limit resets whenever the order, a filter, or the query changes, so a new view never inherits the previous scroll depth.

-----

<a id="understand-the-implementation"></a>

@local/session-hub README · Understand the implementation：<details>
<summary>Implementation internals — click to expand</summary>

The bundle is one browser package with a two-line Host half and no build step; `client.js` is plain JavaScript that registers a module-loader factory whose id equals the package name. The Host `apply` exists only so the row resolves.

@local/session-hub README · KV Cache effect：None. The page's data never enters a provider request.

-----

<a id="known-limitations-and-deferred-work"></a>

